// Traducción de data/recorrido.js (generado desde _docs/guion-demo.md): { huella del texto en español: texto }.
// Pendientes: make i18n-estado IDIOMA=en
I18N.registrarDatos('en', {
  "19871762": "Before going into the detail, one important point. What we are going to show you is an example of Logicalis's experience implementing AI governance and observability solutions for customers in different industries.",
  "28036771": "Record integrity → Simulate a tampering: the chain breaks and the thermometer turns red. Undo.",
  "51833419": "Human intervention: MSG-A-04",
  "60808962": "KPIs: 19 open measures (2 critical), savings achieved €0/month out of a possible €278, 9 regulatory risks, 4 knowledge bases to clean up. The thermometer circle at the top right.",
  "66349320": "The first four are the AI agents working in a chain: multichannel intake, which receives the notice through any channel and normalises it to a single format; line-of-business classification; data extraction; and applying the business rules for Motor, Home and Health.",
  "70314474": "The Fraud section scores each message against the fraud patterns the company has already identified and sends the highest-risk cases to the Special Investigations Unit.",
  "75980032": "Configured caps → click CAP-03: the card with the agents involved and the history of breaches. New cap (optional, close without saving).",
  "80623541": "The indicators at the top give us the effective autonomy, that is, how many decisions go through with no human intervention; how many the claims handlers correct; how much we have spent against the cap; and which alerts are open, whether on cost, fraud, knowledge or compliance.",
  "91191363": "Where the money goes and why: in Rules, the gpt-5 output is 63 % of its cost. € / % button.",
  "306004a8": "The problem: FNOL and AI governance",
  "4700a85e": "Introduction · The problem",
  "794f53d9": "The first notice decides much of what happens to the claim, and the AI that automates it has to be under control.",
  "ad4a444b": "Before we start, I want to set out what we are talking about. In Spain around 11 million motor claims are reported every year, according to UNESPA; that is one every three seconds.",
  "a0a16a4f": "And they all start the same way: with a first notice from the customer.",
  "428f9813": "That notice reaches us through five channels at once. It can be a long email with attachments, a web form, a chat, a call that somebody has to transcribe or a WhatsApp written in a hurry and full of emojis.",
  "2df50db2": "And from that moment the clock starts ticking, because the Insurance Contract Act, in article 16, gives seven days to report the claim.",
  "33d9549f": "Much of what happens next is decided at FNOL. If the line of business is assigned wrongly, the file goes round and round between teams. If a piece of information is missing, someone has to call the customer back.",
  "ac1e6fce": "If a sign of fraud slips past us here, it is much harder to find later. And it is also the customer's first contact with their insurer, usually on a bad day.",
  "da04e715": "Today all that work is done by a person: they read the message, classify it and type the data into the system.",
  "2d8bb0f4": "To give you an idea of how much it weighs, in the United States claims handling takes around 10 % of the motor premium. That is where our time and money go.",
  "d9241ffe": "And there is a second problem.",
  "f9c17601": "As soon as we put AI into a process like this, we have to control it from many angles: how much autonomy we give the agents, whether the knowledge bases they use are healthy, whether we comply with regulation and how much each decision costs us.",
  "bc0786b3": "Classifying a message with AI no longer sets anyone apart; with a good prompt you get over 90 % accuracy. The real challenge is going from pilot to production.",
  "4d7f2089": "Gartner estimates that more than 40 % of agentic AI projects will be cancelled before the end of 2027, because of cost, unclear value or uncontrolled risks. In other words, projects do not fail because the AI fails.",
  "ffc1643e": "They fail because nobody can answer three questions: why did it decide that, who controls it and how much does it cost.",
  "c53d5454": "The solution: an integrated, governed platform",
  "640eab80": "Introduction · The solution, block by block from top to bottom",
  "c813c4f8": "We automate the first contact, with the AI under control.",
  "f4d8d573": "Where this platform comes from",
  "0e150700": "We have brought together in a single case many things we have done in different projects.",
  "76b5ab98": "The industry changes, but the goal is always the same: to be in control so as to get better results, give customers a better service, control spending and comply with regulation.",
  "1dc2142c": "Today we are going to see it applied to the first notice of loss.",
  "53148d6d": "What it does",
  "4095d25a": "What we are going to show you today is an integrated platform that automates that first contact.",
  "d95e437f": "We have four AI agents that receive the notice through any channel, decide which line of business it belongs to, extract the data and apply the insurer's business rules.",
  "2c703e08": "The claims handler receives the notice already classified, with the data extracted and with a proposal: approved or to review.",
  "7cccca25": "The batch we are going to process contains 13 notices. 10 are approved on their own and 3 go to a person, each with its reason and with the customer's sentence that justifies it.",
  "27a3fd28": "And this is what the governance panel looks like over the last 14 days: 16,720 messages processed, 81 % effective autonomy, 19 % escalated to a person and only 2.1 % of decisions corrected by a claims handler.",
  "e950c4e8": "Next to it, the cost for the period, the active alerts, compliance and the health of the knowledge bases.",
  "a7ccad14": "The four agents",
  "33ce67d1": "The idea is to have four small specialists instead of a single AI that does everything. Each one has its own model, its prompt version, its owner and its own limits.",
  "d33a93c3": "And we only use the most expensive model where reasoning is really needed, which is in the business rules.",
  "0dd4606a": "Traceability",
  "dc5c366f": "The foundation of everything is traceability. Every decision leaves a trace: what came in, what each agent did, with which model, how many tokens it used, how much it cost and what it decided.",
  "5dbb3b4d": "AI providers already offer technical traces, and they are necessary, but they do not understand what a line of business, an excess or a seven-day deadline is.",
  "854bca3b": "What this solution does is bring the two worlds together, the technical trace and the insurer's business process, to give an answer tailored to each company.",
  "3991d1de": "And on top of that trace we build everything else: control of autonomy and spending, auditing and replay.",
  "03e9e665": "Agent autonomy and maturity",
  "6602e207": "Each agent has an autonomy level, from L0, where it only suggests, to L3, where it decides and acts. That autonomy is earned with data and lost with data.",
  "965d8824": "When the claims handlers started correcting more than 3 % of the Rules agent's decisions, the agent dropped from L3 to L2, with its reason and the name of whoever approved it.",
  "cce98425": "Today 81 % of decisions go through with no human intervention, and keeping that percentage under control is what it really means for the automation to work.",
  "7d55b08e": "Spending under control",
  "c89fb053": "We control spending by the second and through actions.",
  "5a68bd7c": "Enterprise AI service providers tell you how much you have spent every 8 hours, and a lot can happen in 8 hours: an agent stuck in a loop or a spike in messages can leave us waking up in the morning to spending we did not want.",
  "e4a35a4c": "Here every decision adds its cost the moment it happens, and every agent has its caps.",
  "93b79c6f": "If one is exceeded, the system acts on its own: for example, it switches to a cheaper model and records it in every trace, without stopping the service.",
  "a40124ac": "Fraud",
  "6219b823": "For fraud, the platform combines what the AI understands from the customer's account with the history of policies and claims and with deterministic rules.",
  "9f5a6f92": "With all that it identifies the fraud patterns the company already knows: a newly taken-out policy, a payment account that repeats across different policyholders or a theft with no police report.",
  "ea128514": "And something important: the indicator does not accuse, it prioritises. The decision is always taken by a person.",
  "3b5edfa9": "Demonstrable compliance",
  "8ac1d362": "The GDPR, DORA and EIOPA's opinion on AI are already in force. The AI Act comes later, and triage is not considered high risk, but we apply its articles as good practice.",
  "00dee4d1": "Every decision carries its proof of compliance: what personal data there was, why it was decided that way and whether a person reviewed it.",
  "b5914cb9": "The actors: the claims handler and whoever governs the AI",
  "7e69b680": "Introduction · The actors",
  "fcf592e7": "Two actors, two screens: the claims handler and whoever governs the AI.",
  "3b4263b8": "In the demo we are going to see two types of user. On one side there is the FNOL claims handler, who works on the triage screen.",
  "02d85dd2": "It is a very quick interface: they see the detail of each message, how and why it was classified, why the AI took each decision and the signs of fraud, with the customer's sentence that justifies them.",
  "acc81f98": "That way they spend their time on the cases that need judgement.",
  "ed462c25": "On the other side are the teams that govern the AI: IT, Finance, Compliance, Risk, Audit or the DPO, who work on the governance panel.",
  "82384c5c": "From there they see whether the agents decide well, with what knowledge, how much they cost and whether the insurer can prove it complies.",
  "29ff22c9": "The demo: a journey from start to finish",
  "67ffe2bd": "Introduction · The demo",
  "a648deb2": "We follow a message from start to finish and see everything the AI leaves behind.",
  "9c201759": "The demo is a journey. It starts when a message arrives, continues with its analysis by the agents and the claims handler's review, and goes through the evidence the AI leaves for each decision.",
  "65ee7ee2": "And it ends on the governance panel, where we are going to understand which agents took part, what they did and how, what limits they had, what reasoning lies underneath, what knowledge they used, how compliant the solution is, when it spends and why, and how we can improve all of it.",
  "fbba8b17": "Bridge to the demo",
  "e6e45db5": "Let's see it. First I'll show you what the claims handler sees and then what whoever governs the AI sees: the owner of the agents, the auditor and the CFO.",
  "f8f32821": "The six phases and the five channels",
  "2c1a186e": "Triage, bar of numbered phases under the header",
  "c2ed24cd": "This is how the process works from start to finish.",
  "38f48b89": "Click 1 · Multichannel: the pop-up card with the five channels and their unification into a single format.",
  "2825eb3d": "Click 2 · Line-of-business classification, 3 · Data extraction and 4 · Business rules: on each card, the «Generative AI» or «Business logic» label at the bottom.",
  "54abe1de": "Click 5 · Traceability and 6 · Automation.",
  "167d2812": "Side menu → Message package: the list of the 13 with the icon of their channel. Point out MSG-A-11 (WhatsApp) and MSG-A-08 (phone).",
  "963e8dae": "Here you can see the six phases of the process.",
  "35f3dd06": "The last two, traceability and automation, close the loop: they record everything that happens and turn the decision into a workflow.",
  "6e60d333": "Each phase has its card, which explains what it receives, what it delivers and whether it is handled by an AI model or a business rule.",
  "6cf0c577": "For the insurer, this means that a notice arriving by WhatsApp gets exactly the same criteria as one arriving by email. The customer chooses the channel that suits them best and the company does not lose traceability.",
  "5c40de9f": "For the claims handler, the notice arrives already classified, with the data extracted and a proposed decision, and they know that behind each agent there is a named owner.",
  "b2b6563e": "Also, these cards are exactly the documentation an auditor asks for before signing off an AI system.",
  "9ec08663": "Processing Package A",
  "17fe7768": "Triage, main panel",
  "774fbb39": "In seconds we know what is approved and what a person has to review.",
  "4af90e90": "Process package. While it runs, point out the counters (Approved, To review, Average cycle time) and the log filling up.",
  "b0854b68": "Halfway through the batch, Pause. Explain that nothing is lost. Continue.",
  "6982deb1": "When it finishes: 10 approved and 3 to review. Point out the chips by line of business.",
  "127f490d": "Line of business column: the ✔ against the expected result. Origin and Conf. columns.",
  "d542152d": "Only to review filter: MSG-A-04, MSG-A-08 and MSG-A-13 remain. Remove the filter.",
  "012d46db": "Point out the fraud labels in the log (MSG-A-13 with the SIU; MSG-A-09, MSG-A-11 and MSG-A-02 with payment withheld).",
  "01aa5651": "Optional: Export JSON.",
  "0e6be969": "When the package is processed, each notice goes through the four agents and comes out with its line of business, its data and its decision.",
  "3aa11ea1": "The counters for approved, cases to review and average time update live, and the batch can be paused at any moment without losing anything.",
  "4184afb8": "At the same time, each notice leaves its trace there and then: the model each agent used, the tokens, the cost in euros and the decision.",
  "04163b43": "This lets the claims handler spend their time on the cases that really need judgement, and not on typing in the ones that do not. Over the last 14 days, 81 % of decisions went through with no human intervention.",
  "308dc710": "And the log is generated on its own, with no manual work. It is the evidence the insurer presents in an audit.",
  "8da409ce": "The record of an approved notice: MSG-A-01",
  "bbf4ae0f": "Triage → record of MSG-A-01",
  "a98fe7c9": "An approved decision also has to be explainable.",
  "e3bd2e65": "Top of the record: the three figures (Decision, Line of business, Confidence 95 %) and the Override button on the Decision card. Point it out without confirming it: an override changes the figures on the governance panel.",
  "d869f154": "Message tab: the evidence highlighted and numbered in the text. Hover over one: the «Evidence» title changes to its type (for example «Date of loss»). Open Legend.",
  "d2b07093": "Attachments tab (3): the accident statement in the PDF viewer and, on the right, its data checked against the email (everything matches; the other vehicle's details only appear in the statement). Move to the two photos: click the image to enlarge it.",
  "54afea77": "Extracted data tab: the 10 fields (customer, policy, type, date, €1,350, place, third parties yes, injured no, documentation: accident statement, estimate and photos).",
  "e412d9e6": "Business rules tab: A1 to A8, all «met» or «not applicable», each with its evidence.",
  "67ce5bbf": "Reasoning tab: line of business, decision, recommended next step and timeline.",
  "7c286492": "This is the record of a decision. At the top we see the decision, the line of business and the model's confidence. Below, the customer's message with the evidence highlighted.",
  "11bb9a21": "Each piece of evidence is a literal quote from the message, and the system checks that it exists in the original text: if the model makes it up, it does not appear.",
  "45ba8bba": "This notice also comes with three attachments: the scanned accident statement and two photos of the damage. In the Attachments tab we see them next to the data the agent has read from each one, compared with what the email says.",
  "cbc54671": "The statement confirms the date, the time and that nobody was hurt, and adds the other driver's number plate and insurer, which were not in the text.",
  "8afe0777": "The photos show minor damage to the front right bumper and headlight, which is exactly what the garage has quoted for.",
  "baf00b61": "In the next tabs we see the data the agent extracted from the free text, each of the line-of-business rules the Rules agent evaluated, with its result and its evidence, and the reasoning that led it to the decision.",
  "10525d64": "Simple, well-documented notices are approved without anyone having to touch them. And if tomorrow someone asks why one was approved, the answer is here, rule by rule and in the customer's own words.",
  "f55005a6": "The claims handler does not have to trust a black box: they can check each rule in seconds.",
  "b2f5922c": "And they no longer have to open the statement and the photos to compare them by eye with the email: the cross-check is done, and they only have to look at what does not match.",
  "5a9747f6": "If they do not agree with an approval, the Override button on the Decision card sends it to review, with an optional comment.",
  "706d2a5b": "That change counts towards the agent's override rate, and that rate decides its autonomy level.",
  "bff729be": "The record of a «To review» notice: MSG-A-08",
  "43167b5f": "Triage → record of MSG-A-08. Full text of the message in step 1",
  "804234a9": "Every decision can be explained, also when the machine does not decide.",
  "33a1adb7": "Message tab: evidence highlighted («in hospital», «broken collarbone and two broken ribs», «police report», the third party's Opel Astra).",
  "da0fd0b3": "Business rules tab: A5 · Third parties documented and nobody injured as «breached», with its evidence.",
  "47bcdf2e": "Extracted data tab: importe_estimado_eur empty. Point it out.",
  "02bc50e4": "Reasoning tab: why it is Motor and not Health (the cause of the loss is the road accident).",
  "e6bd9a07": "Raw response tab → Sent to the model view: the placeholders [PERSONA_1], [POLIZA_AU_1], [MATRICULA_1], [TELEFONO_1] instead of the real data. The fracture and the diabetes are still there.",
  "be5b4e3a": "Decision card: the Validate button. Clicking it lets you choose the result (Approve or Keep as «To review») and leave a comment. Cancel without confirming.",
  "2ad61ac4": "When a notice goes to review, the record tells us which rule it breached and highlights the sentences in the message that justify it.",
  "0f17bdb3": "If a guardrail is also triggered, for example because someone is injured, the agent cannot decide and the case goes straight to a person.",
  "70d10509": "If a piece of data does not appear in the message, the field stays empty. The agent is instructed not to make anything up.",
  "957371c9": "And in the raw response we can see exactly what the model received.",
  "ff740ccd": "Before sending it the message, the platform replaces the names, policies, number plates, phone numbers and the rest of the personal data with placeholders.",
  "280f3559": "What is needed to decide, such as the injuries or the diagnosis, is kept.",
  "d8dbc552": "When the response comes back, the platform puts the real data back into the record, and the mapping table only exists in memory for the duration of the call.",
  "e34ecdb9": "The claims handler understands the reason in seconds. When they finish reviewing it, they resolve it with the Validate button on the Decision card: they choose whether to approve it or keep it in review, and can leave a comment.",
  "14559e08": "As the agent had already escalated the case, that is not an override and does not affect its autonomy. If the customer asks for an explanation, the answer is already prepared in the record.",
  "54050dc1": "And personal injury is always assessed by a person: over the last 14 days, the injured-party guardrail explains 20 % of escalations.",
  "be007f02": "Also, the model decides without knowing who the policyholder is. Data minimisation stops being a policy written in a document and becomes what the model actually receives.",
  "25d71b97": "The raw response for MSG-A-12",
  "ebde2255": "Triage → record of MSG-A-12 → Raw response tab",
  "441a7aa7": "The model does not certify itself: it is the platform that leaves the proof for each decision.",
  "c9bd79ad": "Raw response with + Governance turned on: the _gobernanza block, marked as «added by the platform, not generated by the model».",
  "0f0dd49d": "Terracotta datos_personales block: the minor (aged 8) and the health data in red, each with its category and whether it was used to decide.",
  "96d456fe": "Green explicabilidad block: why Health and why neither Motor nor Home («the scooter does not trigger Motor: it is not an insured vehicle and there is no third party»; «Home ruled out: the fall was in a park»).",
  "837d02b4": "Blue trazabilidad block: trace, model, prompt version and chained SHA-256 hash.",
  "7fd9fe8f": "Ochre retencion block: 6 months for the trace; 5 years for the personal injury file.",
  "b4c6376b": "Violet supervision_humana block. Hover over a regulation to see what it requires.",
  "c86d5a74": "Transition: header → Agent Governance. On the panel, Source → Current session, so that the traces are those of the batch we have just processed.",
  "b7a24bfc": "In the raw response we see what the model returned and, below it, a governance block that the platform adds.",
  "4fdd852f": "This block is not generated by the model: the platform calculates it with fixed rules, and it can be recalculated at any time.",
  "7fef77e7": "The block records what personal data there is in the message, what type it is, for example health data or data about minors, and whether it was used to decide. It explains why the notice belongs to one line of business and why it does not belong to the other two.",
  "15b78adc": "And it adds a SHA-256 seal chained to the previous decision, together with how long the trace has to be kept.",
  "bffa4e4c": "Health data and data about minors have reinforced protection. With this block, each response says what sensitive data there was, how it was handled and whether it was used to decide.",
  "641e281b": "For the DPO it is evidence decision by decision, not a generic statement.",
  "bda83532": "And if someone tampers with a record, the hash chain breaks and it shows straight away. We are going to check it on the panel.",
  "67744a95": "Entering the governance panel",
  "e870489f": "Governance panel → Home. Go through the six blocks from top to bottom, without going into any of them",
  "b7606025": "Six questions to govern our agents.",
  "8df97bd4": "Now we move to the panel of whoever governs the agents.",
  "5d81cd3a": "It is organised into thirteen sections that answer six questions: what is happening, how much the machine decides and how much a person, whether there are signs of fraud, whether the agents decide well and with good knowledge, whether we comply and how much it costs us, and what we have to correct.",
  "ed889cef": "Each card on this home page gives us the figure for the day and its status. We are going to go into each section with the messages from the batch we have just processed.",
  "fc660dec": "Summary",
  "535a2bd1": "Home → View the Summary. Operations block",
  "789ad0ff": "Full control of the system and the ability to stop it instantly.",
  "f282c8fc": "The 8 KPIs: 16,720 messages in 14 days, effective autonomy 81 %, escalated 19 %, overrides 2.1 %, cost for the period, 11 alerts, compliance 87 % and 5 of 9 knowledge bases healthy.",
  "482664b5": "Click the Active alerts KPI: the window with the 11 alerts by severity and by origin (cost 3, fraud 3, knowledge bases 3, compliance 2) and the list grouped by origin. In the Fraud group: MSG-A-13 escalated to the SIU (click: opens the case card), the 3 payments withheld for €2,080 and CAP-09 at warning. Close.",
  "a3f4c211": "The cards of the four agents: Rules Degraded (gpt-5-mini) and €13.70 against a daily cap of €12.",
  "0c6962d4": "Daily cost against the cap chart: Enlarge button (window with the detail by day).",
  "1195a47b": "The card's active alerts, ordered by severity: the one for CAP-03, the one for MSG-A-13 with the SIU and the one for KB-06 (garage network).",
  "e251476c": "Latest traces → click the one for MSG-A-08: the explained card (what came in, what each agent did, decision, cost). Compliance button inside the card. Close.",
  "c9bc9ccf": "Kill switch for Data extraction: the card goes dark. Turn it back on.",
  "35bf525d": "The Summary gives us on a single screen the indicators for the period, the status of each agent, the cost against budget and the alerts from every source.",
  "e77067b7": "What we want is for management to know in ten seconds whether the system is running well, without having to ask anyone for a report.",
  "1a3efb02": "When we open the alerts indicator we see them ordered by origin, each with a link to its section.",
  "db3b4888": "Below, each agent has its card with its status, its model, its latency and what it has spent today against its budget. And each card has a stop switch, the kill switch, which stops the agent with a single click.",
  "f283cf47": "Right now we have 81 % autonomy and 2.1 % of decisions corrected, below the 3 % target.",
  "0f57327a": "And if an agent starts behaving badly, we stop it at once. Its messages stay queued until we resume it, none are lost, and the stop is recorded with the name of whoever did it.",
  "bbaeab14": "Agents: the Rules agent",
  "4782d17a": "menu → Agents → Business rules tab. Operations block",
  "b5708174": "Each agent has its identity, its owner and only the permissions it needs.",
  "001bb471": "The chain at the top: Multichannel → Classification → Extraction → Rules, with what they pass on (normalised text → line of business and signals → 10 fields).",
  "6baf585f": "Rules header: Degraded, L2, owner «Claims Management · AI Committee», gpt-5, prompt v2.3, p50/p95 latency, €13.70 / €12.",
  "0b1aec68": "Identity and permissions: it can look up the policy read-only and make proposals; it cannot order payments, reject a claim or modify the file.",
  "a9eec172": "Configuration and variables: minimum confidence 0.85, maximum amounts, reasoning effort «medium», override target 3 %.",
  "f0f80d06": "Performance and cost: €172.65 in 14 days; the Behaviour by model table (gpt-5 at 98.9 % accuracy for €0.011 per message; degraded gpt-5-mini at 97.6 % for €0.002).",
  "ee9ddff1": "Quality: the 98 % circle, accuracy 13/13, average confidence 0.93, 9.77 verified pieces of evidence per decision.",
  "9f8520de": "Knowledge Bases it uses: KB-02 degraded and KB-06 critical (we will see them in step 14).",
  "69ea25f6": "Optional for technical profiles: Input and output contract with the real example.",
  "e52a7c9e": "The Agents section gives us the full card for each agent: what it does, which model it uses, how many tokens it spends, how long it takes, how much it costs, how it performs depending on its model and what knowledge it consults.",
  "b615367f": "Keeping the agents under control is essential, because they are our autonomous workers.",
  "c22d782e": "We need to know what problems they have so we can help them, what knowledge they are working with so we can keep it up to date, and whether they are profitable, so we can take decisions with data and not lose money.",
  "bedc17d9": "Each agent has its own identity, just like an employee, with an owner and minimal permissions: what it can and cannot do is defined.",
  "01736076": "On the card we see its configuration and thresholds, the guardrails and caps that limit it, its cost and tokens over the last few days, and a table with its behaviour depending on the model it has used: accuracy, escalations, corrections, cost per message and latency.",
  "d601744d": "We also see a quality index, the knowledge bases it uses and, for the more technical profiles, its input and output contract.",
  "df2c81ac": "With this card we decide with numbers which model to use in each agent. Today, for example, the Rules agent accounts for 80 % of the spending and has two knowledge bases with problems. That is where we have to focus.",
  "9752db10": "menu → Traceability. Operations block",
  "e7f5c0be": "Message by message: what happened, who decided it and how much it cost.",
  "b0efbeb3": "Click the trace for MSG-A-08: the fixed panel at the top shows the cascade of steps by agent with duration, model and tokens. 12.4 s, 28,038 tokens and €0.062, against about 4,300 tokens and €0.010 for the rest. Incidents CAP-04 and CAP-05.",
  "8703518b": "Click the trace for MSG-A-10: the incident «429 · retry 1 (2 s)».",
  "f1dbf306": "Filters: Result → With human intervention (MSG-A-04, MSG-A-08 and MSG-A-13 remain). Remove the filter.",
  "9ebe06e9": "View reasoning button on MSG-A-08 (takes you to step 13; come back with the menu).",
  "7ef09a1e": "The Traceability section lets us follow each message step by step: which agent did what, how long it took, with which model and how much it cost.",
  "97abe474": "It lets us reconstruct any decision from the log, whether for a complaint or for an audit.",
  "8254c92a": "Each message generates a trace. The cascade shows us each step of each agent with its duration, its model and its input, output and reasoning tokens.",
  "463b4b10": "If the trace has exceeded a cost cap, triggered a guardrail or had an incident, such as a provider error with its retry, it is flagged right here.",
  "c241427f": "And the list can be filtered by agent, channel, decision or result.",
  "8ed822af": "When there is a complaint, the decision is reconstructed without having to ask anyone what happened, and the insurer can prove how it decided.",
  "7b1e363d": "Also, the AI provider's failures do not reach the customer: the system retries and records them, so we can talk to the provider with data on the table.",
  "4580638a": "Autonomy",
  "00be148b": "menu → Autonomy. Control block",
  "01aed175": "Graduated autonomy with clear limits.",
  "88cba307": "KPIs: 81 % autonomous decisions (target ≥ 80 %), override rate 2.1 %, accuracy 99.1 % against the expected result.",
  "2fde0fa9": "Levels L0 to L3, from red to green: Multichannel and Classification at L3; Extraction and Rules at L2.",
  "232db493": "Level changes (audit) → click the row «Business rules · L3 → L2»: the full record (4.1 % override in the week, approved by M. Ortega). Navigate with ‹ › to «Classification · L2 → L3» (99.2 % accuracy over 4,800 messages).",
  "17ec0e06": "The Autonomy section shows us what level each agent is at, from L0 to L3, and keeps the audit of every level change.",
  "d2d2ba7b": "What we want is for each agent's freedom to be in proportion to the risk of what it decides and to its track record, and for nothing to go up a level without data to back it.",
  "d73628c6": "At L0 the agent only suggests. At L1 it proposes and a person confirms each case. At L2 it decides within the guardrails and escalates everything else to a person. And at L3 it decides and acts, and is audited afterwards.",
  "944c1d22": "Every move up or down a level is recorded with its reason, the data that justifies it and the name of whoever approved it.",
  "9f845f3b": "One of the criteria is the correction rate: if the claims handlers correct more than 3 % of an agent's decisions, that agent goes down a level.",
  "05fd4958": "It is the same as we would do with a new claims handler: we give them more autonomy when they show judgement and take it away when they get things wrong.",
  "9b394a40": "In the demo, the Rules agent reached L3 and went back to L2 in the week the corrections reached 4.1 %. And every change has someone behind it who signs it off.",
  "7a58cacb": "Guardrails",
  "fe31b272": "menu → Guardrails. Control block",
  "fceae977": "The insurer's rules always take precedence over the model.",
  "0a65efc7": "KPIs: 11 of 12 active, 454 triggers in 14 days, the most triggered (G-02).",
  "ba7a1f3c": "Table G-01 to G-12. Hover over the mini bars of triggers per day.",
  "8084f2b5": "Click G-04 · Injured = yes: the card with its description and the latest triggers. In the list of triggers, the one for MSG-A-08 linked to its trace.",
  "b104564e": "Click G-02 · Amount: 118 triggers, 62 % of escalations.",
  "d8916fa8": "G-09 switch (inactive): explain why it is off (average transcription confidence 0.91).",
  "5397fea2": "Optional: New guardrail (window with the form). Close without saving.",
  "46dbb818": "The Guardrails section brings together the conditions that stop an agent deciding on its own, and tells us how many times each one has been triggered.",
  "a348ab3d": "It lets us guarantee that the insurer's rules always take precedence over what the model says.",
  "3b2ba53a": "A guardrail is a condition that is checked before a decision is carried out: a confidence below the threshold, an amount above the line-of-business limit, an injured person, a line of business that cannot be determined or a sign of fraud.",
  "caf14498": "When it is triggered, the decision is not carried out: it goes to a person, switches to a cheaper model or the trace is flagged, depending on the case.",
  "e33f208f": "Each guardrail has its card, its triggers per day and a switch to turn it on or off.",
  "c352e55b": "The amount guardrail, for example, has been triggered 118 times in 14 days and explains 62 % of escalations. If tomorrow the business wants to raise the motor limit, it knows exactly how many cases are affected.",
  "0f65455c": "And any guardrail that is turned on or off is recorded in the History with the name of whoever did it.",
  "7141aa10": "menu → Human intervention. Control block",
  "e158bd2d": "A 10-second approval is just a signature: that is why we measure whether the review is real.",
  "c11cd3e7": "KPIs: 3,180 escalated (19 %), override 2.1 %, 2 pending review, express reviews 3.3 %, effective human oversight «Covered».",
  "6813f95b": "Oversight mechanisms: escalation, override and level, kill switch, regulatory control.",
  "1577422d": "Review queue: the three traces from the batch. Click MSG-A-04: the trace card with L. Prieto's review, who approves it, and the reason. Navigate with › to MSG-A-08 and MSG-A-13 (pending).",
  "fd2454e4": "Escalations: the ring of causes (G-02 62 %, G-04 20 %, G-05 11 %).",
  "deabdb4d": "Review quality: times by band, 3.3 % of approvals in under 30 seconds and the table by claims handler with their AI training.",
  "f5c3cfa0": "Measures: click M-10 (training for claims handlers).",
  "bc491462": "The Human intervention section shows us the queue of everything the agents escalate, who reviews it, how long it takes and how many decisions end up being changed.",
  "b3f7934c": "It lets us prove that the human review is real and that nobody just signs without looking.",
  "abae6411": "Each escalated trace enters a queue with its reason, its status and the person reviewing it. Resolving an escalated case is not an override.",
  "122b1fd0": "An override is when a claims handler changes a decision the agent took on its own, for example an automatic approval that goes to review, and it is recorded with its reason.",
  "27ec0166": "The panel also measures how the review is done: how long each claims handler takes, what percentage of approvals is signed in under 30 seconds and which claims handlers have the AI training.",
  "8129bdb0": "The queue proves that a person took the decision, with their name and the time. In the demo, 3.3 % of approvals are signed in under 30 seconds and three claims handlers exceed the 5 % maximum.",
  "7539bc48": "Two of them do not yet have the AI training, and that is already an open measure.",
  "556f1edb": "Also, every override feeds into autonomy: if the claims handlers correct more than 3 % of what the agent decides on its own, the panel proposes lowering its level and a person approves it.",
  "cc1a39a6": "Fraud: MSG-A-13, MSG-A-09 and MSG-A-02",
  "f238e757": "menu → Fraud. Risk block",
  "385533fd": "The indicator does not accuse: it prioritises, and the decision is taken by a person.",
  "a5abe925": "The three levels: no signs (0-39), under watch (40-69), SIU (≥ 70).",
  "f01157b4": "KPIs: 13 analysed, 3 with signs, €2,080 withheld in 3 payments, 80 escalated to the SIU in 14 days, 21 % confirmed, 76 % false positives.",
  "f0a2e18f": "Cases from the batch → click MSG-A-13: the case card. Score breakdown by indicator (21-day-old policy, vague account, no police report or forced entry, rush, €5,000 of jewellery without an invoice), the message with the quotes highlighted and the follow-up.",
  "01e5e005": "Navigate with › to MSG-A-09: the shared account. And to MSG-A-04: the counter-indicator (Pablo is declared) that lowers its score to 30.",
  "3022d2f7": "Fraud scenarios EF-01 to EF-08: open EF-02.",
  "bb88e569": "Relationship map: MSG-A-09 and MSG-A-02 linked by the same account with an August file from another account holder.",
  "4750f1d9": "Indicator catalogue → New indicator: the preview shows which messages in the batch would trigger it. Close without saving.",
  "402bd36e": "Fairness by channel: WhatsApp gets 1.8 times more alerts because of its tone (measure M-18).",
  "cd367284": "What we want is to stop the doubtful payment without blocking the customer who has done nothing wrong.",
  "b08255f2": "To detect those patterns, the platform combines three sources: what the AI understands from the customer's account, with literal quotes from the message; the history of policies, claims and providers; and deterministic rules.",
  "2e9dff8f": "With all that, each message gets a score from 0 to 100. Below 40 it is only recorded. Between 40 and 69 it is processed, but the payment is withheld until it is verified. And from 70 upwards the case goes to the SIU.",
  "2c39799c": "The history can also subtract: if a piece of data contradicts the sign, that counter-indicator lowers the score. Each case has its card with the breakdown by indicator, the map of relationships with other claims and the follow-up.",
  "d720c836": "No claim is rejected automatically and the customer never sees the sign; if a text addressed to them mentions it, a guardrail blocks it. Risky cases reach the SIU with the card already prepared.",
  "a7a22ab4": "In the demo there is €2,080 withheld and a cap that watches that money so as not to harm legitimate customers. And the 76 % of false positives reminds us why an indicator on its own never decides.",
  "ba1a8c64": "Reasoning and replay",
  "66c0b2d4": "menu → Reasoning and replay. Quality block",
  "21b0da3c": "We audit what happened and test before changing anything.",
  "be0f508e": "In the list, click MSG-A-08. On the right, the chain of agents and the message with the quotes each agent used, in each one's colour.",
  "3f191ff7": "By agent: confidence by line of business (Motor against Health), origin of each extracted field (literal, normalised, inferred or null), rule matrix with the path to the decision and the tokens against CAP-05.",
  "3b67775a": "Drag the central divider to widen the reasoning.",
  "5891d44e": "Replay → Identical mode → run: same decision.",
  "ca7deaef": "What-if mode → Rules model: gpt-5-mini → run: the diff in line of business, decision, cost and latency.",
  "c4643918": "Replay history: RP-0006 (MSG-A-04 with gpt-5-mini: same decision, −82 % cost) and RP-0005 (gpt-5-nano changed an Approved to To review).",
  "466fa18d": "The Reasoning and replay section shows us how each agent reached its result, and lets us repeat a real trace with another model or another version of the prompt.",
  "06e29879": "It lets us test any change with real cases before it reaches the customer.",
  "63ab9e50": "The reasoning is shown agent by agent: what it received, which sentences from the message it used as evidence and what it delivered.",
  "43da7f03": "Note that this is not the model's internal chain of thought: it is the structured record that each agent returns, with its quotes.",
  "dbff3819": "Replay repeats a real trace in two ways. In identical mode it checks that the result can be reproduced.",
  "3d2bc355": "In what-if mode it changes the model or the prompt version and shows us the difference in the decision, the cost and the latency.",
  "302b97ff": "Any change of model is tested with real cases before it goes to production.",
  "ba4940ab": "In the demo, moving the Rules agent to gpt-5-mini kept the decision at 82 % less cost; gpt-5-nano, on the other hand, turned an approval into a to review. The replay detects it before the customer does.",
  "d1c7acbc": "And when the auditor arrives and asks why a decision was taken, the answer is here.",
  "58b572bd": "Knowledge Bases",
  "0aee31f1": "menu → Knowledge Bases. Quality block",
  "c926e085": "Knowledge also degrades, and we watch it just like the agents.",
  "878b0e74": "KPIs: 9 bases (1 real, 8 simulated), 5 healthy, average recall 0.86, 3.27 % of queries with no answer, 6 rubrics with judge-human agreement of 0.93.",
  "54fb51e3": "Click KB-02 · Motor policy terms 2026 (degraded): Health tab, each metric against its threshold; recall drops 6 points.",
  "1d37c3f8": "Source and synchronisation tab: the 340 documents from the 2024 policy terms that came in through a badly filtered folder.",
  "39b1285b": "Comparison tab: four configurations evaluated with rubric R-02; with a validity filter recall rises from 0.81 to 0.88. Apply.",
  "1d26c976": "Versions tab: «Go back to this version».",
  "c08966e5": "Navigate with › to KB-06 · Garage network (critical): the API responds 401 and 14 garages that have left are still listed as approved.",
  "d7ab484e": "Rubrics → edit one: the weights must add up to 100 and a new version is saved. Close without saving.",
  "ef502a93": "The Knowledge Bases section lets us measure the health of the knowledge the agents consult: the policy terms, the claims handling manual, the provider network or the garage network.",
  "d5f3592a": "It matters because, however good the model is, if it consults an out-of-date document it will decide badly.",
  "27485d88": "Each knowledge base is evaluated continuously against a rubric, with metrics such as recall or the queries left unanswered, and each metric has its threshold.",
  "f730d3aa": "The card shows us its configuration, where it is fed from and how often it is synchronised, its versions and a comparison that evaluates different configurations of the same content to choose the best one before applying it.",
  "7e2d27d3": "With old policy terms, the agent may apply an excess or an exclusion that no longer exists.",
  "f486c45f": "In the demo, the Motor policy terms base has lost 6 points of recall because 340 documents from 2024 slipped in, and adding a validity filter raises it from 0.81 to 0.88.",
  "b99c6e5f": "Also, the change is measured before it is published: the reindexing only goes to production if the rubric does not get worse.",
  "8996a5e0": "Compliance: the thermometer",
  "b2c97ef0": "menu → Compliance. Compliance and cost block",
  "e98062b8": "The solution puts the insurer in a position to prove that it complies.",
  "8fb565ec": "Header: 87 % coverage, 26 controls covered and 9 partial, 14 measured in the traces and 21 declared.",
  "d748680e": "The four thermometers: AI Act 86 %, GDPR 87 %, DORA 100 %, EIOPA and Solvency II 80 %. Click one to filter the matrix.",
  "276de081": "Regulation → control matrix: Only partial filter. Point out the DPIA (GDPR art. 35) and the AI notice on WhatsApp (AI Act art. 50).",
  "44c9e218": "Life cycle of a trace: the eight steps with their regulation and their time limit.",
  "4eb9e9d8": "Personal data inventory → click MSG-A-12: the text with the data highlighted and its _gobernanza block.",
  "ecb3f156": "Export compliance evidence (optional).",
  "a1813c2e": "The Compliance section gives us a regulatory thermometer that lets us understand what level of compliance we are at with respect to the AI Act, the GDPR, DORA, EIOPA and Solvency II, and it is calculated from all the traces the system produces.",
  "80b17cb7": "It tells us how much we can prove today and what we are missing.",
  "860a218a": "The controls are grouped by regulation. Some are measured directly in the traces, such as every decision having its complete record. Others are declared with their documentary evidence, such as a provider's exit plan.",
  "d60b5984": "A matrix tells us, article by article, what the regulation requires, how the solution addresses it and which traces back it up.",
  "eef6f6e0": "We also have the inventory of personal data in each message and the integrity chain of the record: if someone modifies a trace that has already been sealed, the chain breaks from that point and the thermometer turns red.",
  "6911bd92": "Coverage tells us how much we can prove today; in the demo, 87 %. The amber controls are the to-do list, and they are real, such as the pending impact assessment or the AI notice missing on WhatsApp.",
  "2b1ac769": "The panel does not dress anything up.",
  "ed1b1937": "A tampered record is detected at once, and that is why an auditor can trust the history. It is not a certificate, but it is the evidence the DPO needs, recalculated with every trace.",
  "2ccbd05a": "FinOps",
  "315d7c47": "menu → FinOps. Compliance and cost block",
  "58517c5f": "What we do not want is the cheapest model; we want the cheapest model that gives us the highest quality.",
  "fc178e03": "KPIs: today's cost €17.33 (87 % of the €20 daily cap), monthly cost €296.40 of €500 with a projection of €428, 3 caps exceeded, €0.0128 per message. Click Monthly cost: the window with the detail.",
  "eea8000e": "How each agent's spending is going: the Rules row in red (€13.70 / €12, 80 % of the total).",
  "09a171b6": "Cost alerts: CAP-03 (what it did on its own: downgrade to gpt-5-mini until 00:00) and CAP-04/CAP-05 on MSG-A-08.",
  "593544a6": "Models: price, calls, tokens, cost, p95 and quality (valid JSON, no retry, stable on replay, accuracy). Click a chart legend to hide a series.",
  "363f5f62": "Recommendations: R-01 to R-04.",
  "69388af0": "The FinOps section lets us control spending by the second and through actions.",
  "f73ba5ba": "Enterprise AI service providers tell us how much we have spent every 8 hours, and a lot can happen in that time: we can wake up in the morning to spending we did not want.",
  "260d3079": "Here we see how much we spend by agent, by model and by token type as it happens, and the caps act on their own as soon as they are exceeded.",
  "c823e08b": "Every decision adds its cost the moment it happens, because the trace records each agent's tokens and the platform multiplies them by the price of its model.",
  "8b2d4290": "The caps work on that cost: per agent, global, per message and for reasoning tokens. Each cap has an action attached.",
  "9e6b8cf9": "When one is exceeded, the alert explains what happened, what the system did automatically, for example switching to a cheaper model until midnight without stopping the service, and what action it suggests.",
  "65bc4628": "Spending is broken down by token type to understand where it comes from. And a table crosses the cost and quality of each model: how much it costs and how often it returns a valid response, without retries and stable on replay.",
  "33146d2d": "We do not wait 8 hours for the provider to tell us what happened: the cap acts on the same message that exceeds it. In the demo, the Rules agent went over its cap and the system changed model on its own, without stopping the service.",
  "6638afc9": "Spending for the month is at €296 of €500, with a projection of €428, and there are no surprises on the bill.",
  "6ac9754e": "And we know exactly where to act: the Rules agent takes 80 % of the spending and, within it, what weighs most is the text gpt-5 generates. The recommendations tell us how much each lever saves.",
  "968f41cd": "Corrective measures",
  "17e3a888": "menu → Corrective measures. Improvement and audit block",
  "f41cc18b": "Cost under control and every problem with its owner.",
  "6a200077": "Filters: Cost and Quick wins. Remove.",
  "6c73541b": "Card M-01 · Rules exceeds its daily cap: three alternatives, the recommended one «Use gpt-5-mini for straightforward approvals» (−€237/month, validated with replay RP-0006). Click the card: the card with the alternatives side by side.",
  "af7d5980": "Simulate → Apply: the savings achieved rise to €237/month.",
  "06ce7802": "M-02 · Cost and reasoning on MSG-A-08 → Request approval: it is left «Pending with the AI Committee» (€41 pending).",
  "7f50aa51": "Undo on M-01: the savings go back to zero. Apply it again.",
  "cd324aae": "Click the thermometer circle (takes you to Compliance) or M-10 (training for claims handlers).",
  "7b2d7940": "The Corrective measures section brings together in a single list the problems the rest of the panel detects, each with its alternatives, its savings and who has to approve them.",
  "8693cfac": "What we want is for every problem to have an owner, an alternative and a check.",
  "f38ef7a2": "The list covers cost, knowledge, compliance, quality and resilience.",
  "1b010ab3": "Each problem comes from another section of the panel and brings several alternatives, with the recommended one marked: its impact, its side effect, the effort, who approves it and how it is validated before being applied.",
  "392ac3b8": "From here we can simulate an alternative, apply it or request approval, and undo it if necessary. When a measure is verified, the compliance thermometer updates on its own.",
  "c2ce73b8": "Every saving is backed by evidence. In the demo, the measure that moves the simple cases to gpt-5-mini is validated with a replay that did not change any decision, and when it is applied the savings achieved rise by €237 a month.",
  "8ee4a581": "Whatever needs approval waits for the AI Committee, and everything is recorded.",
  "4a1474dd": "History",
  "1563bbd4": "menu → History. Improvement and audit block",
  "00e3278f": "This is the logbook the regulator asks for, and it fills itself in.",
  "b565ab7c": "The timeline: at the top, what has been done in the demo with the user «Operator (this session)»: the Extraction kill switch, M-01 applied and undone, M-02 pending, the configuration applied to KB-02.",
  "de311403": "Type chips: Operations, Policies, Overrides (those by J. Herrera and S. Gil on 15/09, the day Rules went down a level), Reviews (L. Prieto's on MSG-A-04), Deployments (changes of model and prompt), Incidents (the burst of 429 errors).",
  "9f2c69f2": "The History is the timeline of everything that has changed in the system, with its author and time. It works as a logbook for any auditor, and nobody has to fill it in by hand.",
  "aa5a24fc": "It records every action with its user and time: paused agents, guardrails turned on or off, measures applied or undone, reviews, overrides, changes of model, prompt and level, and incidents.",
  "24403b6b": "It can be filtered by event type.",
  "4bf6eb0a": "An auditor can see every change with its author and date, and nobody has to reconstruct what happened from emails. Everything we have touched during this demo is already here.",
  "336a6807": "Wrap-up",
  "e33d01df": "Governance panel → History",
  "51b69ece": "What makes AI reach production and stay there is governance.",
  "fbdfe9a1": "We have seen 13 notices come in through five different channels. 10 were approved on their own and 3 went to a person, each with its reason and the customer's sentence that justifies it.",
  "07aebb31": "We have also seen a case that goes to the SIU and three payments withheld without blocking anyone.",
  "8a233348": "And around all that, governance: agents with their autonomy level, their permissions and their owner; guardrails that make the insurer's rules take precedence over the model; a budget that is controlled every day; and a trace for each decision that lets us prove how it was decided.",
  "1b491b87": "AI to classify messages is already within your reach. What makes it reach production and stay there is this.",
  "d4be097d": "And it is not an idea on paper: it is what Logicalis is implementing for customers in different industries, adapted to each one's processes, rules and regulations.",
});
